findings.description:
`pending-review` / `review-failed` are values of the per-slice `SliceStatus`. At pre-slice-plan there is no slice and no slice plan yet. The design says to "extend the no-active-slice / pre-slice-plan path … Set `pending-review` / `review-failed` accordingly", but it never says:
- which entity carries that status, or where it shows up in `getStatus()`;
- which index goes to `detectDocuments(projectPath, sliceIndex, 'arch')`. The arch review is named by the initiative/arch index, not a slice index;
- what the "arch file exists, no slice plan" check is when a project has several initiatives.

This boundary only arrived with the 244 fold-in, and it is the one with a different insertion point (240-arch, Anticipated Slices: "different insertion point in the cascade"). Fix: give it its own short subsection that covers status ownership, how the index is resolved, and the recommendation shape. Add a matching fixture to the test list. The `arch` fixtures are currently optional ("`arch`/`slice`").
